& \frac{\sqrt{5} \times \sqrt{2}}{\mathrm{ L}+\mathrm{r}}=\frac{\sqrt{2} \times \sqrt{2}}{\mathrm{r}}=\frac{2}{\mathrm{r}} \\
& \sqrt{5} \times \sqrt{2} \times \mathrm{r}=2(\mathrm{ L}+\mathrm{r}) \\
